			<div class="content" id="post-content-4106595">
									

<p>This is wacky and offbeat in exactly the right way. The idea that Kendal mint cake is inherently anomalous and requires the Foundation to monopolise its production, the concept of sales graphs correlating with mountain ranges to alter them, and especially &quot;the phylum Eldritch&quot; &#8230; it's all great, even if the monster itself is a bit bland by necessity.</p>
<p>I do think the Lovecraft connection feels kind of shoehorned, and the fact that the sales graphs can alter the topography isn't clearly established prior to the &quot;Update&quot; section, but on the whole this is a great entry.</p>

